WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.550
Let's say I put this on the board.

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.180
X plus three fourths equals one.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.530
Before anybody picks up a pencil, I ask,

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.330
“How sure are you that you can solve
this equation on your own?”

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.040
One student tells me they're pretty sure.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:17.180
They subtract three fourths from both sides,
but get the fraction part wrong.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.060
Another student says they're barely sure at all

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.740
and gets one fourth, with work that shows
exactly why.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.250
If I only look at who got it right,

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.670
I miss something I could use
to help both students.
